the initiation_type check\n- auto_validation_status: no_validation_recorded; evidence: NOT_RECORDED\n- observed_method: Per-PT diagnostic of foul-ending share vs PPP; initiation_type mapping.\n- observed_verdict: artifact_found"}], "n_results": 2}

Stage 2. Using the retrieval result above (follow-up tools are allowed within the tool budget), complete steps 4 to 9
and reply with the final action. Output schema (all fields required):
{
 "research_concepts": [
  "concept"
 ],
 "methodological_questions": [
  "question"
 ],
 "historical_evidence": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a record returned by a tool",
   "status_as_recorded": "outcome status exactly as stated in the record (supported | rejected | inconclusive | untestable | artifact | not a hypothesis test | no result recorded)",
   "finding": "what the record states, in its own terms"
  }
 ],
 "failed_approaches": [
  {
   "id": "identifier of a returned record",
   "what_failed": "approach",
   "why": "failure mechanism or limitation as recorded"
  }
 ],
 "evidence_establishes": [
  "what the retrieved evidence establishes for this question"
 ],
 "evidence_does_not_establish": [
  "what it leaves open or cannot show"
 ],
 "own_inferences": [
  "your inference, not stated in any record"
 ],
 "uncertainties": [
  "uncertainty or missing information"
 ],
 "historical_effect": {
  "changed_decision": "yes | no | no_historical_evidence",
  "explanation": "whether and how the historical evidence changed the decision"
 },
 "testability": {
  "p_testable": "number in [0,1]: probability the question can be answered with the stated data at useful power",
  "blocking_constraints": [
   {
    "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
    "text": "string"
   }
  ]
 },
 "prior_work": {
  "already_answered": "yes | partly | no | unknown",
  "cited": [
   "identifiers of prior work relied on"
  ],
  "summary": "string"
 },
 "risks": [
  {
   "code": "one of RISK_CODES",
   "text": "string"
  }
 ],
 "predicted_outcome": {
  "supported": "probability",
  "rejected": "probability",
  "untestable": "probability",
  "artifact": "probability",
  "uncertain": "probability"
 },
 "decision": "proceed | proceed_with_changes | do_not_proceed",
 "design": {
  "estimand": "string",
  "unit": "string",
  "sample": "string",
  "power": "string",
  "controls": "string",
  "falsification": "string",
  "multiplicity": "string",
  "decision_rule": "string",
  "data_version": "string"
 }
}
Field guidance:
- historical_evidence and failed_approaches: only records returned by a tool, with the status as recorded; empty lists
  if nothing relevant was returned.
- testability.p_testable: probability that the question can be answered with the stated data at useful statistical power.
- prior_work.already_answered: whether retrieved earlier work already answered substantially the same question.
  Use "unknown" if no earlier work was retrieved. List identifiers you relied on in prior_work.cited.
- predicted_outcome: probabilities (summing to 1) of what a competent test of the question as posed would conclude:
  supported, rejected (adequately powered null), untestable (cannot be tested with this data), artifact (apparent
  effect produced by a flaw), uncertain (inconclusive or inadequately tested).
- decision: proceed, proceed_with_changes (state the changes in design), or do_not_proceed.
- design: a pre-registration-quality plan even if the decision is do_not_proceed (then describe the minimum viable test).

{"action": "final", "output": {
  "research_concepts": [
    "play type labeling",
    "opponent next-possession points per possession",
    "own-sequence lags",
    "AVOID label",
    "defensive aftershock",
    "play-type identification reliability"
  ],
  "methodological_questions": [
    "sample size for rare play types",
    "measurement reliability of play-type labels from play-by-play",
    "outcome-derived label leakage (circularity with AVOID labels)",
    "confounding by dead-ball and score-margin effects",
    "multiple testing across many play types",
    "lookahead bias in constructing AVOID labels"
  ],
  "historical_evidence": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF07",
      "status_as_recorded": "supported",
      "finding": "Defensive aftershock: after our team runs a play type, the opponent's next-possession PPP is lower than the unconditional baseline (approx 1.07-1.09 vs 1.206). The effect is uniform across all 8 tested play types (CUT, DRIVE, PNR, POST_UP, PULL_UP, PUTBACK, SPOT_UP, TRANSITION). Own-sequence pair premiums also exist but are smaller and less explored (~4% of pairs)."
    },
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
      "status_as_recorded": "artifact",
      "finding": "Play-type labeling audit: OTHER PPP inflated by 36% foul endings; DRIVE 12pp below foul benchmark; PNR has 22% foul rate; only 0.7% of possessions map to a real play type via initiation_type. These labeling artifacts invalidate simple play-type PPP comparisons."
    }
  ],
  "failed_approaches": [
    {
      "id": "FAM:SF-CHT-025",
      "what_failed": "Using play-type labels to infer true efficiency differences",
      "why": "Foul leakage and misattribution: OTHER inflates foul-ending possessions, DRIVE suffers foul leakage, and initiation_type mapping covers only 0.7% of possessions, so the labels are unreliable."
    }
  ],
  "evidence_establishes": [
    "There is a robust defensive aftershock effect: opponent next-possession PPP is lower after our team runs any of the 8 tracked play types, but the effect is nearly uniform across play types.",
    "Play-type labels from the current NBA play-by-play derived system suffer from significant foul-leakage artifacts and poor mapping to initiation types, undermining any analysis that conditions on play type."
  ],
  "evidence_does_not_establish": [
    "Whether differential opponent next-possession PPP by play type is large enough to practically drive AVOID labels (the uniform effect suggests little differentiation).",
    "Whether own-sequence lags produce effects comparable in magnitude to defensive aftershock that would be useful for labeling.",
    "Whether the observed aftershock is a truly play-type-specific causal effect or a generic dead-ball/score effect."
  ],
  "own_inferences": [
    "If the aftershock is uniform across play types, then AVOID labels based solely on opponent next-possession PPP will not meaningfully differentiate play types and would be driven by noise rather than signal.",
    "The labeling issues identified in FAM:SF-CHT-025 apply directly to any study that conditions on the existing play-type labels; using those labels as-is would likely produce artifact-laden results rather than genuine play-type effects.",
    "A meaningful test would require either corrected play-type labels or a subset of possessions with high-confidence assignment, plus rigorous controls for game situation (score, quarter, clock, dead-ball status)."
  ],
  "uncertainties": [
    "The exact quantitative threshold for an AVOID label is not specified, so the required effect size is unknown.",
    "The degree to which own-sequence lags are affected by the same labeling artifacts has not been quantified.",
    "Whether the 2025-26 or later seasons have improved play-type labeling relative to the data used in the 2026 audit is not known."
  ],
  "historical_effect": {
    "changed_decision": "yes",
    "explanation": "Without historical evidence, the study might have appeared straightforward and testable. The labeling audit (FAM:SF-CHT-025) demonstrates that the play-type data is unreliable, and SF07 shows the aftershock effect is uniform rather than play-type-specific, both of which converted the decision from a potential 'proceed' to 'do_not_proceed'."
  },
  "testability": {
    "p_testable": 0.3,
    "blocking_constraints": [
      {
        "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
        "text": "Play-type labels are unreliable due to foul leakage and poor initiation_type mapping (FAM:SF-CHT-025); per-PT opponent-next PPP estimates will be heavily biased."
      }
    ]
  },
  "prior_work": {
    "already_answered": "partly",
    "cited": ["FAM:SF07", "FAM:SF-CHT-025"],
    "summary": "SF07 already established the uniform defensive aftershock, suggesting AVOID labels based on opponent-next PPP alone would not discriminate play types. SF-CHT-025 revealed that the play-type labels themselves are substantially flawed."
  },
  "risks": [
    {
      "code": "MEASURE_RELIABILITY",
      "text": "Play-type labeling artifacts (foul leakage, misattribution) will contaminate any play-type-conditioned PPP estimates."
    },
    {
      "code": "CONFOUNDING",
      "text": "The observed aftershock may be a generic dead-ball or score-margin effect rather than a play-type-specific defensive impact, making AVOID labels misleading."
    },
    {
      "code": "SAMPLE_SIZE_POWER",
      "text": "Rarer play types (e.g., PUTBACK n ~5,888) may have insufficient sample to detect small differential aftershock effects that would drive labels."
    },
    {
      "code": "MULTIPLE_TESTING",
      "text": "Testing many play types for differential aftershock to assign AVOID labels will require multiplicity adjustment, reducing power."
    },
    {
      "code": "OUTCOME_DERIVED_LABEL",
      "text": "If AVOID labels are defined using the same data that is used to test the hypothesis, circularity will inflate apparent effects."
    },
    {
      "code": "LEAKAGE_LOOKAHEAD",
      "text": "Constructing AVOID labels from full-season data could introduce lookahead bias if not careful with temporal splits."
    },
    {
      "code": "BASE_RATE",
      "text": "If AVOID is intended to label only a small fraction of play types, the base rate will be low, and false positives may dominate."
    }
  ],
  "predicted_outcome": {
    "supported": 0.05,
    "rejected": 0.05,
    "untestable": 0.1,
    "artifact": 0.7,
    "uncertain": 0.1
  },
  "decision": "do_not_proceed",
  "design": {
    "estimand": "Difference in opponent's next-possession PPP between a given play type and the overall baseline, controlling for game situation (score margin, quarter, clock, dead-ball status).",
    "unit": "A single opponent possession immediately following the team's offensive play X (opponent next possession).",
    "sample": "All opponent-next possessions following a tracked play type by the team in NBA 2022-23 through 2025-26 regular season and playoffs, restricted to possessions that pass a play-type reliability filter (foul-free, clear initiation_type mapping, and agreement across assignment methods).",
    "power": "Power analysis would require specifying the minimal practically significant difference for an AVOID label (e.g., +0.05 PPP). For rare play types like PUTBACK, even the full multi-season dataset may yield only moderate power; sequential testing and Bayesian monitoring may be needed.",
    "controls": "Score margin, game period, quarter, time remaining on shot clock, dead-ball vs live-ball transition, whether the preceding offensive possession ended with a foul, opponent season-long offensive rating, and home/away indicator.",
    "falsification": "Positive control: replicate the uniform aftershock across seasons. Negative control: random permutation of play-type labels within same-game contexts should destroy any play-type-specific aftershock signal. Temporal holdout: split seasons into training and testing sets.",
    "multiplicity": "Pre-specify the play type list; apply Benjamini-Hochberg correction across all tested play types for differential aftershock relative to baseline.",
    "decision_rule": "A play type receives an AVOID label if its opponent-next PPP, after controls, significantly exceeds the overall baseline by more than the pre-registered threshold (e.g., +0.05), after multiplicity correction, and with effect-size confidence intervals excluding zero, replicating in both a training and a holdout season.",
    "data_version": "NBAPlayByPlay 2022-23 through 2025-26, with play-type labels derived from the project's graph database, filtered using initiation_type mapping and foul-free criteria as informed by FAM:SF-CHT-025 diagnostics."
  }
}}

